one of the questions I get most often  from people in the comments is how can I  be more motivated and disciplined to  train or to work towards my other goals  and this makes sense because really is  the key to unlocking everything else you  want to achieve how do you force  yourself to grind on a business or side  project day in and day out when you  aren't seeing any progress how do you  wake up early in the morning to go to  the gym when you just want to roll over  and go back to sleep if we're going to  be nerdy about it and we are  Batman's only real superpower is his  discipline the answer is that you don't  force yourself you make it awesome you  make it fun you'll be completely honest  with yourself about your goals and about  what makes you feel alive and you work  towards that motivation and discipline  are driven by emotions not logic so if  you're excited by what you're doing it  won't be a chore you need to be  completely honest with yourself then  about what you want to do and what that  looks like you need to be able to  picture it and feel that emotional tug  you need to be excited when you do this  that's your vision or the quote Simon's  neck you're why this will become your  superpower and if you can't motivate  yourself to get up every morning for  that thing then this isn't truly what  you want you need to be more honest with  yourself but then you're going to forget  that vision because whilst the vision is  the inspiring end destination what's  more important of a single step you take  every single day you don't write a book  you write a page every day you don't get  into amazing shape you workout every day  the end result is provision but the  small steps are the goals the concrete  rules that you need to live by because  if you focus on the distant future it's  too disconnected from your reality it's  too easy to put off taking those steps  because you can always do it later it's  hard to stay the course because you  don't see immediate meaningful progress  many people don't even take the first  step because as soon as they do they  introduce the possibility of failure you  can't fail if you focus on those  immediate steps every day as a new  challenge and the macro goal will take  care of itself people who talk about  their grand visions and hopes but won't  take the small boring step so the ones  that never accomplished their aims my  channel now has 50,000 plus subscribers  do you know how many videos I made that  just got a few views each I did hundreds  of thousands of press-ups before I  benched 150 kilograms I can't do that at  the moment but shut up this is meant to  be motivational so how do you stay  focused on that dull grind when you  really  want the glory you make sure that you  enjoy the journey as much as the  destination to remind yourself how that  simple step is helping to make me end  vision of reality you connect the forest  to the trees watch something awesome  inspired before you train a workout that  speaks to those same emotions set  milestones and mini goals create a  feedback loop so that you can see  yourself progressing that might mean  working towards plant or increasing the  way from the barre little by little but  most of all make it awesome train like  Batman work by candle light for a  kettlebell around an abandoned tanker  with synth wave lighting and dubstep  playing in the background it doesn't  matter what other people think it  doesn't matter if it's childish or goofy  as long as you think is awesome if  others try to force you into dull  choices resist don't force yourself to  do boring work as soon as you pick up a  dumbbell or a key you become a warrior  as soon as you start typing and  entrepreneur you're living it right now  so where you end up doesn't matter all  that's left to determine is how awesome  you're going to be  you
 

